{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets (excl. territories) and the 2025 population from the census file's own 'United States' row : how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786912596771},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Find the total farmers markets from the first dataset (excluding territories)\n2. Get the 2025 US population from the second dataset (from the 'United States' row)\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to four decimal places\n4. Provide one confident sentence\n5. Use tools to do any math necessary and not mention unverified facts\n\nFollowing the xorq analyst procedure, I should:\n1. Orient first - check for semantic models and existing aliases\n2. Ingest the data sources if needed\n3. Compute values using xorq_select\n4. Declare obligations and verify with xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the catalog and then ingesting the data sources."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KrN1tdzfjDLNi5revY3gqd","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01SkGkMriL5KyihxKDaSTdyG","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":317,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8177,"totalTokens":8504,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.001585,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01022125,"total":0.01181625},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":169},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912596793,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74yQfNevxcLAWj2wWUt","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01KrN1tdzfjDLNi5revY3gqd","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912600536},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01SkGkMriL5KyihxKDaSTdyG","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912600536},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both datasets. Let me create a build script to read the farmers markets data and the census data, then compute the metric.\n\nI'll need to:\n1. Read the farmers markets CSV and count total (excluding territories)\n2. Read the census CSV and get the US 2025 population\n3. Join them (conceptually) and calculate the per-capita metric\n4. Use xorq_select to get the values and verify them\n\nLet me create a build script that does this.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty, so I'll ingest both datasets and calculate the metric. Let me create a build script:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TrWBvPkmuW4oew3doEQZhT","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nfarmers_markets_url = \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\"\ncensus_url = \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\"\n\n# Read both datasets\nfm_df = xo.deferred_read_csv(farmers_markets_url, storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst\"}))\ncensus_df = xo.deferred_read_csv(census_url, storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst\"}))\n\n# For farmers markets: get total excluding territories\n# Territories typically include PR, GU, VI, AS, MP, etc.\nterritories = ['Puerto Rico', 'Guam', 'Virgin Islands', 'American Samoa', 'Northern Mariana Islands']\nfm_us = fm_df.filter(~fm_df['State'].isin(territories))\nfm_count = fm_us.groupby().aggregate(total_markets=fm_us['Count'].sum())\n\n# For census: get US population for 2025\n# The 'United States' row should have the total\nus_pop = census_df.filter(census_df['NAME'] == 'United States')\nus_pop_2025 = us_pop.select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n\n# Cross join and calculate per capita metric\nmetric = fm_count.join(us_pop_2025, lsuffix='_fm', rsuffix='_pop', how='cross')\nmetric = metric.mutate(per_100k=(metric['total_markets'] / metric['POPESTIMATE2025']) * 100000)\n\nexpr = metric.select('per_100k')\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":698,"cacheRead":8177,"cacheWrite":414,"totalTokens":9303,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0034900000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0008177000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.0005175,"total":0.0048392},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":121},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912600537,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74ygaqDnbs5ykGtFPzU","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01TrWBvPkmuW4oew3doEQZhT","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1311 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912606472},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to build this script and add it to the catalog. Let me run the build command.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018QzCDVNnh8K7DA6i7aS6MY","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-62-iea8tvkh && xorq build .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xo